From: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:39:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/33] ipa: simple: af: Focus on the nearest clear subject of
 a 3x3 zone grid

The focus measure only covered the centre third of the frame, so a
subject off centre, or a centre showing the background, made the lens
focus on the wrong distance.

Add per-zone focus measures to the statistics, a 3x3 grid over the
centre 80% of the frame, filled by the CAMSS IFE statistics. When they
are present the coarse scan covers the whole range and records every
zone, then focuses on the zone with the nearest clear peak among those
standing out at least half as much as the strongest one, the centre
counting 1.5 times, and fine scans that zone only. Without zones the
algorithm is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
